--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
INDICATOR DATA IS LICENSED SEPARATELY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

scan/zbtriage/extensiondata.py lists malicious browser extension IDs (confirmed
entries only, IDs and threat types) from chrome-mal-ids,
https://github.com/mallorybowes/chrome-mal-ids - Copyright (c) 2021-2026 Mallory
Bowes Brown and contributors, licensed CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Changed: names and other fields
left out; generated by tools/gen_extension_list.py.

scan/zbtriage/isdidata.py lists Android app ids flagged as dual-use, stalkerware or
spyware from the Intimate Partner Surveillance Detection (ISDi) project,
https://github.com/stopipv/isdi - Copyright (c) 2018 Cornell University, MIT License.
Some of those entries originate from Echap stalkerware-indicators
(https://github.com/AssoEchap/stalkerware-indicators), licensed CC BY 4.0.
Changed: Android rows only, titles left out; generated by tools/gen_isdi_list.py.

scan/zbtriage/rmmdata.py lists remote-access and monitoring programs, with their
program file names, selected from LOLRMM (https://github.com/magicsword-io/LOLRMM),
the LOLRMM project and contributors, licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (copy in
third_party/lolrmm/LICENSE). Changed: hand-picked entries only (programs that let
someone into this computer), our own names and match patterns, file names that
would point at other software left out; generated by tools/gen_rmmdata.py.

scan/zbtriage/driverdata.py lists file fingerprints (SHA-256, or SHA-1 where no
SHA-256 is given) and file names of Windows drivers known to be vulnerable or
malicious, from LOLDrivers (https://github.com/magicsword-io/LOLDrivers), the
LOLDrivers project and contributors, licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (copy in
third_party/loldrivers/LICENSE). Changed: verified entries only, fingerprints and
one file name each; no driver file is included; generated by tools/gen_driverdata.py.

scan/zbtriage/mvtdata.py holds unmodified copies (compressed) of the indicator files
hosted in mvt-indicators (https://github.com/mvt-project/mvt-indicators),
Copyright (c) 2022 MVT, MIT License (copy in third_party/mvt-indicators/LICENSE).
Generated by tools/gen_mvtdata.py. Files that index only points to in other
repositories are not included; they are downloaded by --update.

The device manufacturer list used by the home network check is downloaded from the
IEEE public listing when you run --update; it is not distributed with this software.
Likewise the known-good lists (MISP warninglists,
https://github.com/MISP/misp-warninglists) are downloaded by --update and not
distributed with this software.

The indicator set in iocs/ is NOT covered by the Apache License above. It is
released into the public domain under CC0 1.0 so that it can be copied into
blocklists, STIX bundles, MISP instances and other tools without friction.
See iocs/LICENSE.md.

iocs/curated_targeted.txt holds file fingerprints and package names copied from
researchers' own indicator files. The selection is CC0; the values remain under
their publishers' terms where those apply, and each notice is kept in that file's
header: ESET and Volexity (BSD-2-Clause), Meta and Palo Alto Networks Unit 42
(MIT), Lookout (Apache License 2.0), Amnesty International (CC BY 2.0) and Cisco
Talos (CC0).

The optional Candiru YARA rules are NOT part of that CC0 indicator grant.
Microsoft Threat Intelligence Center's MAL_DevilsTongue_HijackDll rule is
redistributed from Signature-Base under Detection Rule License 1.1.
Felix Bilstein's win_devilstongue_auto rule is redistributed from Malpedia
under CC BY-SA 4.0. Both rules are unchanged. Author, source and license
attribution are retained in the embedded rules, match details, and
third_party/candiru/. YARA-X itself is a separate optional BSD-3-Clause
dependency, not embedded executable code in this script.

